# Build outputs
target/

# hunk-edit's LMDB staging store (its clap default is `build/hunk-edit`).
# Ignored because the tool is used mid-commit-split: an untracked directory
# appearing in `git status` at the exact moment you are staging two commits is
# noise where noise is most expensive. Override with HUNK_EDIT_STORE.
#
# `branch-merge`'s session store and conflict reports live here too
# (`build/branch-merge/`, ADR 4.8.26d) for the same reason, one flow over: they
# are written mid-integration, when a spurious "uncommitted changes" is most
# expensive. That tool excludes its own state dir by pathspec regardless, so it
# does not depend on this entry — a consumer repo without one still behaves.
#
# `action-batch`'s surface staging mirror is the third tenant
# (`build/action-batch/surfaces/<task>/`, ADR 6.9.26a). A batch child stages
# the intended bytes of an agent-instruction file it cannot write in place, and
# the driver copies them over afterwards; those drafts are written mid-entry,
# when a spurious delta path would land in someone's commit. It moved here from
# under `.git/`, where a headless child's write is refused outright as a
# sensitive file. Like `branch-merge` it carries its own `:!build/action-batch`
# pathspec on every `git status` it runs, so this entry is the belt and not the
# only strap.
/build/

